{"id": "EUVD-2026-76290", "enisaUuid": "d96e8fe8-7dbd-315d-b9d4-31f982c1da76", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: pcxhr: initialize mutexes before requesting threaded IRQ\n\npcxhr_probe() requests pcxhr_threaded_irq() before initializing\nmgr->lock, even though the threaded handler takes that mutex.\n\nInitialize the manager locks before request_threaded_irq() so an\nearly interrupt cannot run against uninitialized mutex state during\nprobe.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:52", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/039602d6ddb1febbb0561b30dab04461f78a1319", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5f405adb0229c9cf64eb3d695c333c92e3d3d4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ede25b7fea0d7487ee8528bf35dc7b9a1cbcd814", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c069b3cfd753d6688ea0271c43553631ab38ce10", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ef9ad82d95dd3c74570d80a689a0570fbc7539e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7cf280fbef5db6310e1b32074c8c34d1ba459796", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c97817e20598e5473094e0e38d1f51f1cf4dfff"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gf23-mfwg-9j7j", "CVE-2026-80967"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c368cee-7217-3e52-b550-9d44495302a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "1c4da01c-6631-3330-aa08-384755c8cf80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "25e3ba06-5318-36fb-9a96-7cdb4e9c0557", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9bef72bdb26e291d6dffb04768741a0e49582666 <6c97817e20598e5473094e0e38d1f51f1cf4dfff"}, {"id": "376b4689-7b93-3dcc-a27a-63326aef530c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"i